@@ -0,0 +1,127 @@
+# Darkroom Mobile: Android UI fork
+
+Based on `togekk39/darktable-android` master
+`ae4139bdf18a5c39f71c24f1fb3eab320c139cc9` (2026-11-26).
+The processing source lock identifies darktable
+`1c4eaea9df6dbe8336449ca297acbb0120d8e968`.
+This is an unofficial development fork, independent of Spektrafilm.
+
+## Workspace
+
+- A fixed top toolbar contains Open, Undo, Redo and Export.
+- The photograph is above its inspector in portrait and beside it in landscape.
+  Drag the separator to resize them. Accessibility progress actions resize the
+  same separator; activating it restores the default ratio. Landscape retains at
+  least 280 dp for controls and 240 dp for the photo.
+- The preview supports pinch/pan, double-tap zoom/fit, a Fit button and expansion
+  into the inspector area. These transformations never enter the pixel pipeline.
+  Native photo-coordinate tools reset/disable preview zoom so their existing
+  geometry mapping remains valid.
+- Light/Color, Detail/Repair and Geometry/Effects retain the complete original
+  tool inventory. Settings opens a full-height application preferences page.
+- Tap the tool name for a searchable category catalog. The separate search
+  button searches names and parameter labels across all categories. Exact
+  native instance IDs and On/Off states are retained. Navigation never enables
+  a tool or creates a native edit.
+- Parameters retain their original controls, ranges and precise number inputs.
+  Numeric drafts now survive tool switches, full-photo view and saved-state
+  restoration. Blending/parametric masks and drawn/repair masks have labeled
+  expandable sections; nothing is removed or merged.
+- Russian app resources cover every translatable shell string. Tool labels use
+  the original Russian darktable MO catalog. Native IDs, values and the native
+  processing locale are unchanged. The existing languages remain selectable.
+- Opening another edited photo from the editor asks before opening the picker.
+  Cancelling that picker leaves the photo intact. The original engine's Cancel
+  is terminal for the session; stopping an operation with a previous photo now
+  explicitly confirms that it will close the session. Finishing an operation
+  automatically removes an obsolete stop dialog.
+
+| Original location | Fork location | Processing behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Actions below preview | Top toolbar | Original callbacks and document pickers |
+| Fixed 50/50 vertical split | Resizable portrait/landscape panes | Presentation only |
+| Category tool dropdown | Searchable category catalog | Exact instance selection, no auto-enable |
+| Cross-category search | Search beside tool selector | Original name/parameter search |
+| Light/color controls, curves, WB | Light/Color inspector | Original controls and native calls |
+| Denoise, sharpening, repair | Detail/Repair inspector | Original controls and native calls |
+| Crop, perspective, lens, effects | Geometry/Effects inspector | Original controls and native calls |
+| Blending/parametric controls | Expandable section in the same tool | All existing parameters retained |
+| Drawn/repair mask controls | Expandable section in the same tool | All existing shapes/nodes retained |
+| Settings in half-screen panel | Full-height Settings | Languages, themes and licenses retained |
+| Export dialog | Top Export button, original dialog | Original full-resolution native export |
+
+## Build with the original processing runtime
+
+The UI fork does **not** rebuild, translate or substitute the native processing
+algorithms. Its engine comes byte-for-byte from the checksum-verified upstream
+APK for the exact Android source revision above. The published APK contains 115
+engine/runtime libraries, one independently pinned AndroidX native library and
+830 runtime data files. The recovered module list is the inventory observed in
+that APK, not proof that every optional desktop module was enabled.
+
+Use JDK 17, Gradle 8.14.4, Android Platform/Build Tools 35 and an official NDK
+providing API 26 AArch64 system stubs. The official wrapper JAR and distribution checksum are included; see
+[README.md](README.md). From the repository root:
+
+```sh
+curl --fail --location \
+  https://github.com/togekk39/darktable-android/releases/download/dev-latest/darktable-android-dev-ae4139b.apk \
+  --output /tmp/darktable-upstream-ae4139b.apk
+python3 android/tools/prepare-upstream-runtime.py \
+  --apk /tmp/darktable-upstream-ae4139b.apk --ndk /absolute/path/to/ndk \
+  --output /absolute/path/to/new-runtime-stage
+cd android
+./gradlew :app:testDevDebugUnitTest :app:testDevReleaseUnitTest \
+  :app:assembleDevRelease :app:lintDevRelease \
+  -PdarktableRuntimeStage=/absolute/path/to/new-runtime-stage
+```
+
+The recovery tool requires upstream APK SHA-256
+`be88cc10e2b9cd9b17ae73eecb49c105ab001d6d0f8a05e2512e5eeb65010d8a`.
+It never rewrites native bytes. It validates the API 26 system stubs separately
+without mixing another NDK's C++/OpenMP runtimes into the APK's original closure.
+The original staging and final APK verifiers check all runtime hashes and ELF
+metadata. For a native source build, use the upstream
+[engine bootstrap instructions](../mobile/dependencies/ENGINE_BOOTSTRAP.md) and
+supply that matching stage instead.
+
+Normal builds now require an explicit engine stage. The old engine-disabled
+route requires `-PdarktableDependencyProbe=true`; it remains explicitly unable
+to open/process photos. An unsigned or dependency-only APK is not this delivery.
+The development release uses application ID `design.komarpunk.darkroom.dev`,
+version 0.2.0/code 2, and a development signing key. It installs beside the
+original author's app. Keep a persistent production key before distributing
+updates beyond this development build.
+
+## Validation boundary
+
+The original revision passed 189 Android/JVM tests, 39 runtime producer/verifier
+checks, four host C adapter tests and an engine-enabled debug build locally.
+The new workspace adds host-executed Compose checks for exact numeric dispatch,
+draft retention, fullscreen/resize, disabled instances, search, narrow Russian
+screens, landscape limits, zoom, import/cancellation and confirmation controls.
+Captures under `app/build/reports/mobile-workspace` render the actual Compose
+view tree with a sample image. They are UI fixtures, not RAW-engine screenshots.
+
+The delivery report records actual final suite results separately. Native bytes
+and data are compared with the original APK; the engine is not run by Robolectric.
+There was no attached Android phone/emulator during this work. No claim is made
+that all RAW cameras, every numeric control's pixel effect, OEM document
+providers, GPU support, performance, cancellation races, process death or
+preview/export color parity have been tested on a device.
+
+Inherited limitations remain: session edits are not a persistent catalog;
+external Android share intents start a new photo session; full desktop preset
+browsing, several automatic pickers, linked liquify/freehand mask workflows and
+optional codecs have the upstream port's documented coverage limits. See
+[control coverage](../mobile/CONTROL_PARITY.md). Existing scalar/dedicated
+controls were not removed to conceal these gaps.
+
+## GitHub fork
+
+The local branch is `feat/mobile-workspace`. Creating a GitHub fork through the
+connected integration returned HTTP 403 `Resource not accessible by integration`.
+No changes were pushed to the author's repository or to Spektrakrill.
+Create the fork in the owning GitHub account, grant the connector access to it,
+and then push the reviewed branch to that new repository. Never force-push an
+existing fork or substitute the author's `master` remote as a writable target.
